body:
### Description

Hi,
i have a strange issue with Matrix which i am not able to find it's root cause. We run a federating server with ~70 members. The server is up for 3 years now and works basically well. Some issue i registered today, as i saw that 3pids do not work correctly in element deskop or web client, but in element android. Registered mail addresses do not appear because API error is thrown (status 404 unrecognized). I do not get it. 

### Steps to reproduce

I checked 

- homeserver.yaml against the refence configuration documentation
- the nginx reverse proxy settings
- the log files

### Homeserver

matrix.fablabchemnitz.de

### Synapse Version

1.78.0

### Installation Method

regular apt repository

### Database

postgresql  12+214ubuntu0.1

### Workers

Single process

### Platform

Ubuntu 18 LTS on a Netcup virtual server

### Configuration

nginx:

```
server {
    listen 80;
    listen [::]:80;
    server_name matrix.fablabchemnitz.de;
    return 301 https://$server_name$request_uri;
}
server {
    listen 443 ssl http2;
    listen [::]:443 ssl http2;
    listen 8448 ssl http2 default_server;
    listen [::]:8448 ssl http2 default_server;
    include /etc/nginx/ssl-config.conf;
    server_name matrix.fablabchemnitz.de;
    access_log /var/log/nginx/matrix.fablabchemnitz.de.access.log;
    error_log /var/log/nginx/matrix.fablabchemnitz.de.error.log;
    client_max_body_size 100M;
     location / {
        default_type "application/json";
        allow all;
	root /var/www/vhosts/matrix.fablabchemnitz.de/;
    }
	location ~ ^(/_matrix|/_synapse/client) {
        proxy_pass http://localhost:8008;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        client_max_body_size 50M;
	proxy_http_version 1.1;
    }
    location ^~ /.well-known/matrix/server {
      return 200 '{"m.server": "matrix.fablabchemnitz.de"}';
      add_header Content-Type application/json;
    }
    location ^~ /.well-known/matrix/client {
      return 200 '{"m.homeserver": {"base_url": "https://matrix.fablabchemnitz.de"},"im.vector.riot.jitsi": {"preferredDomain": "https://jitsi.stadtfabrikanten.org"}}';
      add_header Content-Type application/json;
      add_header "Access-Control-Allow-Origin" *;
    }
}
```

### Relevant log output

var/log/matrix-synapse/homeserver.log says:
```
2023-03-06 20:30:31,096 - synapse.http.server - 107 - INFO - POST-697533 - <XForwardedForRequest at 0x7fc1581b84f0 method='POST' uri='/_matrix/identity/v2/account/register' clientproto='HTTP/1.1' site='8008'> SynapseError: 404 - Unrecognized request
2023-03-06 20:30:31,098 - synapse.access.http.8008 - 460 - INFO - POST-697533 - 80.134.84.181 - 8008 - {None} Processed request: 0.002sec/-0.000sec (0.000sec, 0.000sec) (0.000sec/0.000sec/0) 59B 404 "POST /_matrix/identity/v2/account/register HTTP/1.1" "Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Element/1.11.23 Chrome/108.0.5359.215 Electron/22.2.0 Safari/537.36" [0 dbevts]
```



### Anything else that would be useful to know?

Element Desktop on Fedora 37 as well as https://element.fablabchemnitz.de do not show up registered email addresses, but the mobile client  (v1.5.26) on android does as exspected.

